# {{.ProjectName}}

Go service using Gin, Ent and PostgreSQL, built on go-common.

## Run locally

Run `make setup`, then `make run-local`. The setup command creates `.env` only when it is missing, resolves the Go module, and generates Ent code when schemas exist. `make stop` stops the containers and keeps the database volume.

The Compose stack starts PostgreSQL, applies checked-in migrations, then starts the API. The server exposes `GET /live` for liveness and `GET /ready` for database readiness. Schema changes are created explicitly with `make migrate-diff name=init`, reviewed as SQL, and applied with `make migrate` or the next `make run-local`.

`make migrate-diff` uses the separate PostgreSQL database in the `tools` Compose profile. It does not change the application database. The Atlas Community CLI is pinned in the generated Dockerfile and does not need to be installed on the host.

The default schema has UUIDv7 IDs and timestamps but no business fields. Add fields, validation and persistence mappings in each resource's `ent/schema`, `request.go`, `service.go` and `repository.go`. The scaffold does not add authentication, authorization, tenant isolation, seed data or business rules.

## Project layout

- `cmd/server` starts and shuts down the application.
- `cmd/migrate` inspects or applies checked-in migrations.
- `internal/app` wires configuration, HTTP, health checks and lifecycle.
- `ent/schema` contains Ent schemas; `internal` contains application domains.
